{"unit_id":2,"stage_id":2,"lesson":{"lesson_id":2,"lesson_key":"S2L2","stage_id":2,"title":"Harf-e-Jarr 'Li' (Ke liye): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ","title_i18n":{"hinglish":"Harf-e-Jarr 'Li' (Ke liye): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ","en":"Preposition 'Li-' (For / Belonging to): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ","ur":"حرفِ جر 'لِـ' (کے لیے): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ","hi":"हर्फ़-ए-जर्र 'लि' (के लिए): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ"},"arabic_Focus":"الْكِتَابُ ، اللَّهُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ ، لِلَّهِ","hinglish_Focus":"Kitaab, Allah → Kitaab ke liye, Allah ke liye","page_numbers":"54–55","book_page":54,"sections":[{"id":"sec_hero","type":"hero_header","data":{"arabic":"الْكِتَابُ ، اللَّهُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ ، لِلَّهِ","hinglish":"Kitaab, Allah → Kitaab ke liye, Allah ke liye","arabic_word":"الْكِتَابُ ، اللَّهُ","arabic_combined":"الْكِتَابُ ، اللَّهُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ ، لِلَّهِ","hinglish_word":"Kitaab, Allah","hinglish_combined":"Kitaab, Allah → Kitaab ke liye, Allah ke liye","title_en":"Harf-e-Jarr 'Li' (Ke liye): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ","subtitle":"Unit 2 • Lesson 2 (Book Page 54–55)","transformations":[{"before_ar":"الْكِتَابُ ، اللَّهُ","after_ar":"لِلْكِتَابِ ، لِلَّهِ","before_hi":"Kitaab, Allah","after_hi":"Kitaab ke liye, Allah ke liye"}]}},{"id":"sec_intro_table","type":"intro_table","data":{"title":"S2L2 — Harf-e-Jarr 'Li' (Ke liye): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ: Buniyadi Misaalein","caption":"S2L2 — Harf-e-Jarr 'Li' (Ke liye): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ: Buniyadi Misaalein","headers":["Qaa'ida / Halat","Arabi Misaal","Hinglish Mafhoom"],"rows":[["لِـ + الْـ (Alif gir jata hai)","لِلَّهِ / لِلْكِتَابِ / لِلنَّاسِ / لِلْمُتَّقِينَ","Allah ke liye / Kitaab ke liye / Logon ke liye / Parhezgaron ke liye"],["لِـ + Nakirah (Tanween Zair ـٍ)","لِقَوْمٍ / لِأُمَّةٍ / لِنَفْسٍ","Kisi qom ke liye / Ek ummat ke liye / Kisi jaan ke liye"],["وَلِلَّهِ / فَلِلَّهِ (Muqaddam = Hasr)","الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ / وَلِلَّهِ الْعِزَّةُ","Sab ta'reef Allah ke liye hai / Aur izzat sirf Allah ke liye hai"]]}},{"id":"sec_s2l2_concept","type":"rule_paragraph","data":{"text":"<div class=\"lesson-concept-svg\" style=\"margin:14px 0;padding:12px;border-radius:12px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a,#1e293b);border:1px solid #334155;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 760 190\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <defs>\n    <linearGradient id=\"u123grad\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#0d9488\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#0284c7\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"744\" height=\"174\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0f172a\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"22\" y=\"20\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"url(#u123grad)\"/>\n  <text x=\"97\" y=\"37\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">UNIT 2 • LESSON 2</text>\n  <text x=\"188\" y=\"38\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Harf-e-Jarr 'Li' (Ke liye): الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ (Page 54–55)</text>\n  <rect x=\"24\" y=\"58\" width=\"220\" height=\"68\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#475569\"/>\n  <text x=\"134\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" direction=\"rtl\" font-family=\"Traditional Arabic,Amiri,serif\">الْكِتَابُ ، اللَّهُ</text>\n  <circle cx=\"288\" cy=\"92\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#0d9488\"/>\n  <text x=\"288\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Harf-e-Jarr (لِـ + ـِ)</text>\n  <rect x=\"332\" y=\"58\" width=\"402\" height=\"68\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0f292a\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"533\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#34d399\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" direction=\"rtl\" font-family=\"Traditional Arabic,Amiri,serif\">لِلْكِتَابِ ، لِلَّهِ</text>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"150\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"12.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">• الْكِتَابُ ، اللَّهُ (Kitaab, Allah) se لِلْكِتَابِ ، لِلَّهِ (Kitaab ke liye, Allah ke liye) banta hai.</text>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"170\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">• Huroof-e-Jarr, Inna, Laa, Illaa, Kaana aur Yaa Qur'ani jumlon ki buniyadi chabiyan hain.</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n**Qaa'ida (Pages 54–55):** **`لِـ`** ka matlab **'ke liye'** hai. Iske baad aane wale ism ke neeche **Zair (`ـِ / ـٍ`)** aa jati hai, aur agar lafz ke shuru mein `الْـ` ho toh milate waqt Alif (`ا`) gir jata hai: `الْكِتَابُ ← لِلْكِتَابِ`، `اللَّهُ ← لِلَّهِ`."}},{"id":"sec_s2l2_lbl2","type":"section_label","data":{"text":"Darj zail misaalon par ghaur karein:"}},{"id":"sec_s2l2_r4","type":"rule_paragraph","data":{"text":"Upar di gayi misaalon se wazeh hai ke 'Li' (لِـ) ka matlab 'ke liye' hai. Iske baad aane wale ism par zair (kasrah) aati hai. 'Li' aur iske baad aane wala lafz milkar ek murakkab banaate hain, iss liye unka tarjuma ek saath hota hai. Agar jumle ke aakhir mein kuch nahi toh 'hai' ka izaafa karein."}},{"id":"sec_s2l2_r5","type":"rule_paragraph","data":{"text":"Darj zail aasan Qur'ani ibaarat khud samajh kar tarjuma karein:"}},{"id":"sec_s2l2_g6","type":"two_col_numbered_list","data":{"is_numbered":false,"items":[{"id":"s2l2_g6_w1","arabic":"لِلدِّينِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لدِّينِ</span>","hinglish":"Deen ke liye","translations":{"en":"For the religion","ur":"دین کے لیے","hi":"दीन के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w2","arabic":"لِلنَّبِيِّ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لنَّبِيِّ</span>","hinglish":"Nabi ke liye","translations":{"en":"For the Prophet","ur":"نبی کے لیے","hi":"नबी के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w3","arabic":"لِلرَّحْمَنِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لرَّحْمَنِ</span>","hinglish":"Rahman ke liye","translations":{"en":"For the Most Merciful","ur":"رحمن کے لیے","hi":"रहमान के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w4","arabic":"لِلَّهِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لَّهِ</span>","hinglish":"Allah ke liye","translations":{"en":"For Allah","ur":"اللہ کے لیے","hi":"अल्लाह के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w5","arabic":"لِلْإِيمَانِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْإِيمَانِ</span>","hinglish":"Eemaan ke liye","translations":{"en":"For faith","ur":"ایمان کے لیے","hi":"ईमान के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w6","arabic":"لِلْإِنْسَانِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْإِنْسَانِ</span>","hinglish":"Insaan ke liye","translations":{"en":"For man / mankind","ur":"انسان کے لیے","hi":"इंसान के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w7","arabic":"لِلْإِسْلَامِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْإِسْلَامِ</span>","hinglish":"Islam ke liye","translations":{"en":"For Islam","ur":"اسلام کے لیے","hi":"इस्लाम के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w8","arabic":"لِلْآخِرَةِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْآخِرَةِ</span>","hinglish":"Aakhirat ke liye","translations":{"en":"For the Hereafter","ur":"آخرت کے لیے","hi":"आख़िरत के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w9","arabic":"لِلْكِتَابِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْكِتَابِ</span>","hinglish":"Kitaab ke liye","translations":{"en":"For the Book","ur":"کتاب کے لیے","hi":"किताब के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w10","arabic":"لِلسُّحْتِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لسُّحْتِ</span>","hinglish":"Haraam ke liye","translations":{"en":"For unlawful gain","ur":"حرام مال کے لیے","hi":"हराम (नाजायज़ माल) के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w11","arabic":"لِلْحَقِّ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْحَقِّ</span>","hinglish":"Haq ke liye","translations":{"en":"For the truth","ur":"حق کے لیے","hi":"हक़ के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w12","arabic":"لِلتَّقْوَى","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لتَّقْوَى</span>","hinglish":"Taqwa ke liye","translations":{"en":"For righteousness (Taqwa)","ur":"تقویٰ کے لیے","hi":"तक़वा के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w13","arabic":"لِلشَّهَادَةِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لشَّهَادَةِ</span>","hinglish":"Shahadat ke liye","translations":{"en":"For testimony","ur":"شہادت (گواہی) کے لیے","hi":"शहादत (गवाही) के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w14","arabic":"لِلْغَيْبِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْغَيْبِ</span>","hinglish":"Ghaib ke liye","translations":{"en":"For the unseen","ur":"غیب کے لیے","hi":"ग़ैब के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w15","arabic":"لِلصَّلَاةِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لصَّلَاةِ</span>","hinglish":"Namaz ke liye","translations":{"en":"For prayer","ur":"نماز کے لیے","hi":"नमाज़ के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w16","arabic":"لِلزَّكَاةِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لزَّكَاةِ</span>","hinglish":"Zakat ke liye","translations":{"en":"For Zakah","ur":"زکوٰۃ کے لیے","hi":"ज़कात के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w17","arabic":"لِلنَّاسِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لنَّاسِ</span>","hinglish":"Logon ke liye","translations":{"en":"For the people","ur":"لوگوں کے لیے","hi":"लोगों के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w18","arabic":"لِلْخَيْرِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْخَيْرِ</span>","hinglish":"Bhalai ke liye","translations":{"en":"For goodness / good","ur":"بھلائی کے لیے","hi":"भलाई के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w19","arabic":"لِلْحَرْبِ","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"nonroot\">لِ</span><span class=\"arabic-root\">لْحَرْبِ</span>","hinglish":"Larai ke liye","translations":{"en":"For war","ur":"لڑائی / جنگ کے لیے","hi":"लड़ाई / जंग के लिए"}},{"id":"s2l2_g6_w20","arabic":"لِلْقِتَال